<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Knockdoe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1504">1504</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Knockdoe was fought on 19 August 1504 near Lackagh in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-galway">County Galway</a>, Ireland. The Lord Deputy, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gerald-fitzgerald-8th-earl-of-kildare">Gerald FitzGerald, 8th Earl of Kildare</a>, with allies from the Pale, Ulster and Connacht, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulick-fionn-burke">Ulick Fionn Burke</a> of Clanricarde and his ally Turlough O'Brien of Thomond. It was one of the largest battles fought in Ireland in its era and confirmed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kildare">Kildare</a>'s dominance in Irish politics.</p></div>
